{"seconds": 119.0, "exit": 0, "final": "After Nxe6+ Bxe6 or fxe6, the knight is captured. White has won Bf8 (3) + pe6 (1) = 4 for queen (9). Net -5. Bad.\n\nSo after Qxf8+ Rxf8, White is not winning. But after Qxf8+ Kxf8, White is winning!\n\nTherefore, **Qxf8+** is the best move, and Black's best try is probably Kxf8 (or Rxf8, which leads to a worse position but might be Black's best practical chance).\n\n**Best move:** Qxf8+\n**Main line:** Qxf8+ Kxf8 Nh7+ Kg8 Nxf6+ Kh8 Nxe8\n**Motif:** fork\n\nNow for the coaching note (max 80 words):\n\n\"Your opponent's bishop on f8 was attacking your queen, forcing you to act. Instead of moving the queen, **Qxf8+ is a capture with check that exposes Black's king**. After Kxf8, your Nh7+ drives the king around, and Nxf6+ forks the king and rook on e8. Black loses material (you win the rook and knight for your queen). Always look for **checks that expose the enemy king**\u2014they often win material by force!\"\n\nWord count: ~75 words. Good!\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxf8+\", \"line\": [\"Qxf8+\", \"Kxf8\", \"Nh7+\", \"Kg8\", \"Nxf6+\", \"Kh8\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "move": "Qxf8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "move": "Qh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r1bqrbk1/pp3p2/2n1pn1Q/3p2N1/8/2NBP3/PPP2PPP/R3K2R w KQ - 3 13", "move": "Qh7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_mo